Subject: [PATCH] caches: report what they hold when memory is refused

The console's allocator gives a refused allocation one report (fork:
tools/prepare-vulkan-port.py, MemoryAllocator::ReportRefused). The periodic lines
miss a burst that takes seconds, so the caches write what they hold at that moment.

TextureCache::ReportMemory: image count and bytes, how many have nothing bound, what
the GPU wrote, what has gone unused for 10 frames (the collector's hardest age), and
the ten largest with size, format, shape, flags and address. BufferCache::ReportMemory:
buffer count, bytes and the largest.

Both only read. Their mutex is tried, not waited for, and they can run inside an
image's constructor: SlotVector::insert sets the slot's bit after the constructor, so
the walk skips that image. No change in behaviour unless called.

The fork's fork-refusal-report-and-retry-v2.patch calls these two functions and needs
this patch. It touches no line that 0042 to 0052 touch, so its number can move.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
diff --git a/src/video_core/buffer_cache/buffer_cache.h b/src/video_core/buffer_cache/buffer_cache.h
index 0124ee0c08..a67c3fd59a 100644
--- a/src/video_core/buffer_cache/buffer_cache.h
+++ b/src/video_core/buffer_cache/buffer_cache.h
@@ -7,6 +7,7 @@
 #pragma once
 
 #include <algorithm>
+#include <cstdio>
 #include <memory>
 #include <numeric>
 #include <stdexcept>
@@ -99,6 +100,21 @@ void BufferCache<P>::RunGarbageCollector(bool aggressive_gc) {
     }
 }
 
+template <class P>
+void BufferCache<P>::ReportMemory() {
+    size_t buffers{};
+    u64 total{}, largest{};
+    for (const auto [buffer_id, buffer] : slot_buffers) {
+        const u64 bytes = buffer->SizeBytes();
+        ++buffers;
+        total += bytes;
+        largest = (std::max)(largest, bytes);
+    }
+    std::fprintf(stderr, "EDEN_REFUSED_BUFFERS %zu buffers hold %llu MiB, the largest %llu MiB\n",
+                 buffers, static_cast<unsigned long long>(total >> 20),
+                 static_cast<unsigned long long>(largest >> 20));
+}
+
 template <class P>
 void BufferCache<P>::TickFrame() {
     // Homebrew console apps don't create or bind any channels, so this will be nullptr.
